# Tier Audit - framework / starter / registry boundary

> Status: **Approved** - owner decisions incorporated. Implementation not
> started yet; the order below is the execution sequence once the go-ahead
> is given.
> Origin: nimbus (cloudflare/nimbus) review discussion - apply its "boundary
> test" to this repo so the template's three layers are explicit and any
> misplaced code is found. Nothing implemented yet.

## Why

nimbus splits a docs-site codebase into three tiers, each with one test:

| Tier | Test | Lives in |
|---|---|---|
| Framework | "Am I changing taste or fixing a bug?" - bug = framework | `nimbus-docs` package |
| Starter | "Do changes alter classes/layout or call signatures?" | starter source |
| Registry | "Does every site need this on day 1?" - no = registry | registry, installed on demand |

This repo is a *template* (per `.agents/plan/plan.md`: abstract the hub into a
reusable template). The same split applies, but today the tiers are implicit: a
new adopter (or a coding agent) cannot tell which files are "machinery to
keep" versus "your copy to rewrite" versus "optional hooks". This plan makes
the split explicit, flags real boundary problems, and fixes the small ones.

## Tier definitions for this repo (adopter-friendly names)

Owner decision 1: use friendlier tier names, but keep the descriptions
precise. The nimbus terms are kept in parentheses so anyone who read the
original discussion can map across.

| Tier (this repo) | nimbus term | What lives here | Editing means |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Machinery** | Framework | behavior with (mostly) one correct answer: path/fallback generation, collection wiring, base/locale helpers, route delegation, build validation, sync mechanics | fixing behavior / a bug |
| **Your site** | Starter | visible UI and instance configuration: component look, Nav/Footer/landing layout, global styles, sample copy (`t`/`home`/`productCopy`), the `products` array, sample content | your taste / rebranding |
| **Extensions** | Registry | optional per-product hooks, enabled by a file existing: `product-landing/<slug>.astro`, `product-themes/<slug>.css`, `product-info/<locale>/<slug>.md`, plus `examples/*` sample source repos | opting in / adding optional features |

Boundary test (unchanged): one correct answer -> Machinery; a user might
reasonably want a different answer -> Your site; not needed on day 1 ->
Extensions.

## The audit (findings)

### Framework (mechanism)

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `src/lib/i18n.ts` | locales, base/locale helpers, dictionary *shapes* (see finding A) |
| `src/lib/content.ts` | localized paths + fallback rendering (docs / posts / product-info) |
| `src/lib/docs.ts` | sidebar nav builder |
| `src/lib/feed.ts` | RSS builder |
| `src/lib/product-landing.ts` | landing-override resolver (registry mechanism) |
| `src/lib/heading-ids.mjs`, `src/lib/remark-rewrite-links.mjs` | markdown plugins |
| `src/content.config.ts` | collection generation (zod schemas) |
| `src/pages/**` (all routes) | thin delegation to lib/ |
| `skills/site-content/SKILL.md` | per-hub authoring contract |
| `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` | template CI (build + dual deploy) |

### Starter (taste + instance config)

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `src/components/Layout.astro`, `DocsLayout.astro` | shell composition (behavior noted in finding C) |
| `src/components/Nav.astro`, `Footer.astro`, `PostCard.astro`, `TagPage.astro`, `TableOfContents.astro`, `ThemeToggle.astro`, `LocaleSwitcher.astro`, `ProductLandingDefault.astro` | visible UI |
| `src/config/products.ts` | instance registry (the `Product` interface is framework) |
| `src/content/**` | sample posts / docs / product-info (replaceable) |
| `src/styles/global.css`, `theme.css` | tokens + prose (see finding D) |
| `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, `THEMING.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md` | instance docs |

### Registry (hooks - file-exists-enables)

| Hook | Docs |
|---|---|
| `src/components/product-landing/<slug>.astro` | landing override |
| `src/styles/product-themes/<slug>.css` + barrel line | per-product theme |
| `src/content/product-info/<locale>/<slug>.md` | auto-generated landing data |
| `examples/*` | installable sample source repos + sync skill |

### Findings (boundary problems)

**A. `src/lib/i18n.ts` mixes machinery with instance copy.** The dictionary
tables `t` / `home` / `productCopy` (and `siteName`) are *your copy to
rewrite*; the helpers around them are machinery. Today an adopter must
hand-edit a lib file to rebrand. Fix (approved, decision 2): split the copy
into `src/config/copy.ts`; `i18n.ts` re-exports so import churn is zero;
ARCHITECTURE.md documents "edit `src/config/copy.ts` to rebrand". Cost: one
new file + re-export lines; no behavior change.

**B. `src/config/products.ts`** - the `Product` interface (machinery) and the
array (instance config) live together. Acceptable; document in
ARCHITECTURE.md. No code change.

**C. `Layout.astro` shell** - head behavior (lang, hreflang, base-aware meta,
`data-product`) is framework logic inside a starter-looking component. Today
it is thin and already delegates to `buildAlternates` / `withBase`; extracting
a `buildHeadData()` helper is possible but low value now. Deferred.

**D. CSS contract vs taste** - the `--color-*` token names and `.prose`
typography are the shared contract; token *values* and everything else in
`global.css` are taste. No code change; document the contract in
ARCHITECTURE.md.

**E. Routes / lib - clean.** They already delegate to lib/ and are product-
and locale-agnostic. No change.

## Deliverables

1. **NEW `ARCHITECTURE.md` (repo root)** - the durable tier map. Contents:
   - the three-tier table above (adopter-friendly names + nimbus mapping),
   - the boundary test ("one correct answer -> Machinery; taste -> Your
     site; not needed day 1 -> Extensions"),
   - an "edit X to rebrand / to change behavior / to extend" quick table,
   - the consolidated extension-points table (the three registry hooks +
     `examples/*`), pulled together from today's scattered docs (the
     AGENTS.md product-landing paragraph, THEMING.md, product-info docs).
   `AGENTS.md` gains a short pointer to it (one paragraph; AGENTS.md stays
   conduct/rules, ARCHITECTURE.md is the map).
2. **Finding A fix (in scope, decision 2)** - split the instance copy out of
   `src/lib/i18n.ts` into `src/config/copy.ts` with re-exports, so rebranding
   is an edit to a config file, not a lib file. Zero import churn; no
   behavior change.
3. The extension-points table (see 1) consolidates the currently scattered
   docs.

## Decisions (resolved, owner review)

1. **Tier names: adopter-friendly and precise.** Use "Machinery / Your site /
   Extensions", each described accurately (see the tier table above); nimbus
   terms kept as a mapping.
2. **Finding A: do the split.** `src/config/copy.ts` holds the instance copy;
   `src/lib/i18n.ts` re-exports for zero churn.
3. **Tier map lives in a NEW `ARCHITECTURE.md`** at the repo root; AGENTS.md
   points to it.

## Implementation order

1. Commit 1: NEW `ARCHITECTURE.md` (tier map + extension points) + AGENTS.md
   pointer paragraph (docs only).
2. Commit 2: Finding A split - `src/config/copy.ts` + re-exports in
   `src/lib/i18n.ts` + ARCHITECTURE.md "edit X to rebrand" entry.
3. Verify: `npm run build` passes; `astro check` clean; ARCHITECTURE.md
   matches the tree.

## Verification checklist

- `npm run build` passes with 0 errors.
- ARCHITECTURE.md tier table matches the actual tree (spot-check a few
  files).
- Finding A: `grep` confirms re-exports keep all existing imports working;
  the site renders identically; rebranding now = editing `src/config/copy.ts`.

## Out of scope

- Moving files between tiers beyond the Finding A split (the copy tables
  move Machinery -> Your site by design; no other relocations in v1).
- Extracting a real npm package (no second repo; the template stays a single
  repo - that is a deliberate divergence from nimbus).
- Any behavior change to routes/content/UI.
